.TH NIGHTFALL 6 "2026" "nightfall 1.0.0" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
nightfall \- a living night forest in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nightfall
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B nightfall \-\-play
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B nightfall \-\-gallery
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nightfall
draws a procedural pixel\-art night forest with Unicode half blocks and true colour.
Every scene is composed from a seed: a biome, an archetype, dozens of generated trees,
plants and props. Creatures arrive, follow their own intents (forage, climb, hide in bushes
and hollows, chase, play, sleep) and leave again. Wind travels through the grass in waves.
.PP
Without options it runs as a screensaver: any key quits.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B \-\-play
Playground with a HUD: creature list with their intents, event log and spawn keys.
.TP
.BR \-\-gallery
Browse every shape in the library with its animations and depth map.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-seed " N"
Reproducible scene and behaviour.
.TP
.BI \-\-scene\-time " S"
Compose a new scene every \fIS\fR seconds (0 = never, default 600).
.TP
.BR \-\-biome " auto|off|\fINAME\fR|list"
Biome of the scene. \fBauto\fR picks one by the seed, \fBoff\fR allows everything,
\fBlist\fR prints the available biomes.
.TP
.BI \-\-spawn\-rate " NAME=F " "[NAME=F ...]"
Override spawn chances. The biome's chances add up to 1; \fIF\fR replaces the chance of
that species in the same scale (0 = never).
.TP
.BI \-\-grass\-density " F" ", \-\-grass\-spread " F ", \-\-grass\-zspread " F
Foreground plant density, randomness of the gaps between plants, depth spread (default 1).
.TP
.BI \-\-assets " DIR"
Load \fI.spr\fR assets from \fIDIR\fR instead of the built\-in ones.
.TP
.BI \-\-sheet " OUT.ppm"
Export a sprite sheet of the library (\fB\-\-filter\fR, \fB\-\-depth\fR, \fB\-\-scale\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-snap " OUT.ppm"
Headless simulation (\fB\-\-time\fR, \fB\-\-spawn\fR) and a snapshot.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Short help.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Version.
.SH PLAYGROUND KEYS
.TP
.B q
quit
.TP
.B l
new scene
.TP
.B B
next biome (auto, each biome, off)
.TP
.B h
toggle the HUD
.TP
.B d
show places, paths and links
.TP
.B space
pause
.TP
.BR + " / " \-
simulation speed
.TP
.B n
let the director spawn someone now
.TP
.B r s x o v e g j b c m w p
spawn rabbit, squirrel, fox, owl, bat, eyes, spirit, deer, boar, wildcat, mole, weasel, dhole
.SH GALLERY KEYS
.TP
.BR \(<- " / " \(->
previous / next shape
.TP
.BR \(ua " / " \(da
previous / next animation clip
.TP
.BR space ", " . ", " ,
pause, step forward, step back
.TP
.B z f d o m b p
zoom, flip, depth view, grass in front of / behind the shape, root motion, background, properties
.TP
.B s r
regenerate a procedural shape, reload assets from disk (with \fB\-\-assets\fR)
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A terminal with true colour (24\-bit) and Unicode, e.g. kitty, Alacritty, WezTerm, foot,
GNOME Terminal, Konsole or Windows Terminal. A font with the \(lqupper half block\(rq glyph.
.SH SEE ALSO
The asset format is described in FORMAT.md in the documentation directory.
